00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,480
Right this way, sir.

253
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,440
Okay, Luke, you're coming with me.

254
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:10,180
You got me mixed up with somebody else.

255
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,460
My name's Geraldo.

256
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,660
Not the one you think.

257
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:17,180
Mike, this is, uh, Cherise and Melanie.

258
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:22,280
They're widows. Why don't you take a seat with us, Mike?

259
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:23,380
Come on, don't be rude to the girls.

260
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:26,600
Come on. Please, don't embarrass me.

261
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:31,580
Let's dance. You know, I have a friend who is just your type.

262
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,020
She'll be finished dancing there in 15 minutes.

263
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,740
No, thanks. I'm seeing someone.

264
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:40,440
Hey, Mike, it's okay to flirt.

265
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:41,520
Kate's not gonna know.

266
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:43,640
Who's Kate? Oh, she's the warden.

267
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:45,180
The one who cracks the whip.

268
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:50,260
Whoosh! Excuse me, Eddie, can I borrow your ear for a second?

269
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:54,320
Sure. Tell me.

270
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:57,480
Are you crazy for bringing Luke to a place like this?

271
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,200
Hey, this is a glassy joint.

272
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:00,800
Do you see one spinning tassel?

273
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,960
Eddie, this has nothing to do with spinning tassels.

274
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,460
It has to do with bringing a miner into a nightclub.

275
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:08,500
Mike, are you turning fogie on me?

276
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:12,980
I mean, maybe we can get out of here and go find a hot game of bingo.

277
00:15:14,260 --> 00:15:19,460
And then tomorrow we can put on our dark socks with our plaid shorts and drive

278
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:23,280
around town at two miles an hour with our left blinker going the whole time.

279
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:26,520
Fine. Now, go ahead and make fun of me, Eddie.

280
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:30,380
Now, you may think that I'm an old fogie, but I think you're a bad influence on

281
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:32,460
Luke. Hey, thanks, man.

282
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,800
I'm serious, Eddie.

283
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,920
I don't want you hanging around with him anymore.

284
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,280
Why? Because you're sleazy.

285
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:41,600
You're irresponsible and you're immature.

286
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,380
In fact, I don't even know why I hang out with you.

287
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:47,520
Come on, Eduardo.

288
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:53,760
Let's dance. I'm thinking of having my own talk show.

289
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,020
Excuse me, Robo.

290
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,580
Can I borrow your ear for a second?

291
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:08,480
Morning, sweetheart. Want some breakfast?

292
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:09,540
No, thanks, Mom.

293
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:10,120
I'm not hungry.

294
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:13,300
Mom, would you answer me one question?

295
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:17,560
What on earth possessed you and Dad to ever let me hang out with a jerk like Eddie?

296
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,840
I mean, we did all kinds of bad stuff.

297
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:20,960
We teepee'd houses.

298
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,640
We snuck into an X -rated movie.

299
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:25,120
How X? Well, I don't know.

300
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:27,160
During the opening credits, Eddie hyperventilated.

301
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:31,560
Like, your dad and I let you hang out with Eddie because you liked him.

302
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:32,740
Well, who wouldn't?

303
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:34,600
I mean, the guy was fun and unpredictable.

304
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:38,100
I mean, he's the only guy I knew who could open up a soda bottle with his zipper.

305
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,440
So what's changed?

306
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:45,300
Me. I'm sorry, Mom, but calling a restaurant and paging Seymour Butts doesn't amuse

307
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:49,680
me anymore. Come on, it's not fair to judge Eddie on pranks he pulled five years

308
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:51,320
ago. He did last night.

309
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:56,100
So you think you'd be better off if you and Eddie had never been friends?

310
00:16:56,560 --> 00:17:01,300
Maybe. Mike, you've grown a lot over the past few years.

311
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,600
Maybe Eddie's growth is just a little...

312
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:07,620
Stunted? Come on, you've been friends since you've been kids.

313
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,280
Eddie's part of who you are today.

314
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:10,560
Mom, come on.

315
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,300
I haven't given someone a wedgie in months.

316
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,900
I just wish that he would grow up.

317
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,240
What, and be more like you?

318
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:23,160
Mike, did it ever occur to you if Eddie stopped being Eddie, you might not like him?

319
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:28,000
So you're saying I should just take him or leave him just the way he is?

320
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:33,560
Yeah. I'm sure that deep inside, Eddie wants to grow up.

321
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:37,120
Someday. All right.

322
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:40,740
This is the man who once told a woman, it's okay, I'm a blind brassiere designer.

323
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,860
I just came to get my stuff.

324
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:49,580
Don't worry, I'll throw myself down the stairs.

325
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:55,940
Hey, Eddie, last night, I said a lot of stupid things.

326
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:56,980
Yeah, you got that right.

327
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:58,860
And then again, you did a lot of stupid things.

328
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:00,100
Oh, great apology, Mike.

329
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:02,660
This is a real family ties kind of moment here.

330
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,780
Come on, Andy, what happened to us?

331
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,480
Huh? We were so tight.

332
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:10,640
I mean, we used to laugh at each other's jokes before we even set them.

333
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:13,380
What happened was you started thinking you were better than me.

334
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:15,560
Not better. Different.

335
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:21,080
Better. Different. I mean, I am in a steady loving relationship and you prey on

336
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:28,160
innocent widows. And I have a responsible job and you hock towels at a floating

337
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:34,000
bathhouse. And I'm trying to help raise a 16 -year -old boy so he doesn't turn out

338
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,900
to be someone like me.

339
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:42,090
I have been acting like I'm better than you.

340
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:44,400
Prosecution rests.

341
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:50,560
Eddie, maybe I have been acting like an old fogey.

342
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,340
But listen, I don't have all the answers.

343
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:56,360
I mean, heck, sometimes I'm standing in front of my class and all I want to do is

344
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:59,380
help him make spitballs because you and I made them better than they ever could.

345
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:03,880
Kids today, no attention to quality.

346
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:11,480
Mike, do you think I want to be a towel boy forever?

347
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:17,640
I look at you and I think, compared to me, you really got it together.

348
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:22,940
What if I never make anything in my life, huh?

349
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,380
Oh, come on, Eddie.

350
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:26,340
You got loads of time.

351
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:28,200
You're smart and you're likeable.

352
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:29,460
I mean, it'll happen for you.

353
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:35,060
Am I imagining or we got a bonding thing going here?

354
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:41,160
Hey, I've never seen you this, I don't know, human.

355
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,260
I like it.

356
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,860
Yeah. This is great, huh?

357
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,280
Yeah. Isn't it?

358
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:50,860
Yeah. If you buy this, the widows are gonna eat it up.

359
00:19:56,540 --> 00:20:00,180
Jason, I'm so glad you got back in time to see the video Ben made for Carol.

360
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:01,760
I'm sitting next to Daddy.

361
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:05,040
All right. Now, don't expect too much.

362
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:06,620
I still have to cut three hours out of this.

363
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:08,880
No, just kidding.

364
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,980
He's kidding. Go ahead, honey.

365
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:15,560
Roll it. Dear Carol, I heard you were feeling a little homesick.

366
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:16,900
Well, cheer up.

367
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:20,100
It happens to the best of us when we're away from the people we care about.

368
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:37,820
We hope this video will bring you a smile and remind you of home.

369
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,820
Hi, Carol. Ben was nice enough to take me doing my daily chores.

370
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:46,280
So, honey, you just pretend like you're here doing the laundry with me.

371
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,540
It's my birthday, yes, I'm team.

372
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,480
How many candles do I need?

373
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:54,360
One, two, three years old, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

374
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:55,540
Six years old.

375
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:00,980
That's it. What else do you want me to do?

376
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:03,400
Say goodbye. Goodbye, Carol.

377
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:04,980
Oh, P.S.

378
00:21:05,020 --> 00:21:05,940
Come home quick.

379
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:08,060
Ben's driving me crazy.

380
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:19,580
Now, uh, Carol, uh, in answer to your letter, I miss you too.

381
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:25,140
And I know we've had our differences, but I care about you and I want you to come

382
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:31,140
home soon. Mwah!

383
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,180
That was terrific, honey.

384
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:36,500
We're proud of you, Ben.

385
00:21:36,660 --> 00:21:37,560
Well, it's not finished yet.

386
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,740
I want to get one more shot of the whole family waving to Carol.

387
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,140
That's great. Where's Mike?

388
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:42,760
Come on, come on.

389
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:47,040
What's that? Come on.

390
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:49,020
Let's go, let's go.

391
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:51,200
Shoot it! Come on, Chucky.

392
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:51,880
You don't want that.

393
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,500
Guys, it's 40 degrees out here.

394
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:55,160
What are you doing?

395
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:56,960
I'm beating this little weasel's tail off.

396
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,440
Oh, yeah? Well, we'll see what a weasel is.

397
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:02,140
Miss! Making a plane in their underwear.

398
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,820
I know. Isn't it wonderful?

399
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,160
Give it to Carol.

400
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,900
Hi, Carol. Hi, Carol.

401
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:11,740
Hi, Carol. Hi, Carol.

402
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:12,760
Hi, come back.

403
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:15,840
Come back. Carol.

404
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:52,440
Thank you.
